  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "$x$ and $y$ are two numbers, where $xy=24$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What values could $x$ and $y$ equal if they are whole numbers?\nTry to list as many as possible.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y)=(1,24),(2,12),(3,8),(4,6),(6,4),(8,3),(12,2),(24,1)$.",
          "worked": "List the factor pairs of $24$:\n$$\\begin{align*}1\\times24&=24\\\\2\\times12&=24\\\\3\\times8&=24\\\\4\\times6&=24\\end{align*}$$\nEither factor can be $x$, so the pairs are $(1,24),(2,12),(3,8),(4,6),(6,4),(8,3),(12,2),(24,1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What values could $x$ and $y$ be if they can be decimals, fractions, or whole numbers?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For example, $(x,y)=(0.5,48),(1.5,16),(\\frac23,36)$, as well as the whole-number pairs. There are infinitely many possibilities.",
          "worked": "Examples are $(0.5,48),(1.5,16)$ and $(\\frac23,36)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}0.5(48)&=24\\\\1.5(16)&=24\\\\\\frac23(36)&=24\\end{align*}$$\nThe whole-number pairs also work. There are infinitely many possibilities.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
